Original commit body from eda4309814e739678463fe3e28e3b83c730d6761:

A `path.py:NNN` citation rots silently. The cited code slides downward on any
insertion above it, so the reader lands on unrelated lines with nothing to
signal that anything is wrong. Across docs/adr that had happened at scale:
21 of 241 backticked citations were provably broken before this change (one
past EOF, twenty landing on blank lines), and every non-blank one sampled by
hand had drifted too.

The drift was not cosmetic. ADR-0037 pointed at `to_dict` serialization while
asserting it was the boundary remap. ADR-0040 cited three Edge fields at lines
inside Symbol. ADR-0035's five `make_*_stable_id` citations all landed in one
unrelated function. Two were in status lines, which docs/adr/README.md requires
not to lie: ADR-0028 placed `Edge.is_resolved` 433 lines from where it lives,
ADR-3ccc placed `UsageContext` 219 lines away.

274 references across 29 ADRs now name the symbol instead of the line, in five
notations that had to be found separately: backticked `path:NNN`, bare `:NNN`,
comma-joined lists, unbackticked `path.py:NNN`, and `spec:NNN` / `schema.json:NNN`.
Where the prose already named the right symbol the conversion repaired the
pointer rather than re-addressing it — all 62 such citations were pointing
somewhere else.

Four references whose named code no longer exists are marked historical rather
than re-pointed: ADR-0042's `find_behavior_map` (moved to `survey_io.py` in the
very rename ADR-0042 specifies), ADR-0040's `test_edge_has_evidence_spans`
(deleted with its field), ADR-0041's tier-min relabeling (retired by its own
ruling), ADR-0029's `_find_inherited_initialize` (deleted upstream). Two line
numbers are kept deliberately, both into immutable artifacts.

An AST validator gated the conversion and caught 11 unresolved citations,
four of them symbol names the conversion itself had invented. It also caught
`test_ruby.py::test_rails_routes` in ADR-0008, which was already in `::` form
and already broken — symbol citations rot too, just only on rename rather than
on every insertion above the line. Shipping that validator as an on-demand
checker (deliberately not a CI gate) is WI-kitij.

Verified: 251 symbol citations resolve, 0 unresolved; 0 line references of any
form remain except the two immutable ones; mypy ratchet clean; the three
ADR/spec guards pass (11 tests).

